TITLE='Authentic title "The $10K Savings Formula (That Works on Normal Incomes)" promises a concrete formula with an accessibility qualifier. The script delivers a behavioral bundle (automation, daily breakdown, why, 30-day rule, future value, ego) rather than a single formula. TYPICAL-low (ratio ~0.53) against peers that include the 529K-view affordability outlier and several STRONG passive-income titles. Association only.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White field. Left: the recurring cartoon man in a dark shirt holding a single dollar bill, side-eye smirk. Right: a three-line black headline "THE $10,000 FORMULA" with a curved arrow to stacked cash bundles. Single-bill-to-stack contrast implies growth from small amounts. At 320x180 "$10,000" dominates and remains legible.'
SCRIPT='A behavioral savings script: abandonment hook, loss aversion, automation (payday split, sweep leftovers), $10,000 as $833/month or $27.40/day with swaps, present bias and goal reframing, emotional "why" (Golden Circle), temptation and dopamine, a 30-day "not now" list, future-value thinking, "income minus ego" and an action close. Verified: Save More Tomorrow 3.5% to 13.6% (3.9x) but it is a different mechanism than described; all compounding examples reproduce at 10%. Wrong or unsupported: "3.3x = 330% more" (230%); 90% abandonment, 2019 emotional-savings study and 92% 30-day figure unsourced; 2-week vs 30-day inconsistency. The stored ending is complete.'
